&lt;h3&gt;Your Impact&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;You will contribute to Axon&#39;s product line as part of the Axon Robotics team (formerly Sky-Hero). We are building career-defining, next-generation drones and robots in pursuit of our Moonshot: to cut gun-related deaths between police and the public by 50% over the next 10 years. As a Senior Electrical Engineer, you will advance Axon&#39;s mission to Protect Life by designing and prototyping the electronic boards and systems at the heart of mission-critical robots such as UAVs and UGVs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;This is a senior, hands-on design role within a fast-moving R&amp;amp;D team. You will work on densely populated, tightly packaged, battery-powered systems where size, weight and power constraints make every design decision consequential. Using EDA tools including Altium Designer and Cadence OrCAD/Allegro, you will solve demanding problems across the full breadth of electronics engineering — from analog to digital — and you will design, assemble and debug boards and prototypes as an active contributor to our R&amp;amp;D process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Brussels, Belgium&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;This role is based out of our Brussels office (West Brussels, Rue d&#39;Enghien). Because we are rapidly prototyping confidential hardware, this team works on-site, with some flexibility unless there is an approved workplace accommodation. We believe that in-person collaboration fuels innovation, and our in-office culture is designed to foster meaningful teamwork, mentorship and shared success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Participate in the research and development of our next-generation products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Design schematics and PCBs; test and verify prototypes; and support the Firmware and Software Engineering teams in bringing up new boards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Design and build custom test systems for measuring the performance of our electronics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Test and measure boards, multi-board assemblies and electronic components such as batteries and motors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Support manufacturing and follow up on designs when changes are required due to component obsolescence or unavailability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Electronics Engineering, Electrical Engineering or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;5+ years of industry-leading electronics design experience, with emphasis on densely populated, tightly packaged, battery-powered embedded systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Proficiency in multi-layer PCB layout and/or rigid-flex design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Strong all-round electronics knowledge, from analog to digital&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Knowledge of at least one EDA package: Altium Designer and/or Cadence OrCAD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Awareness of EMC and signal-integrity issues and best practices as they relate to PCB design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Excellent hands-on skills: comfortable assembling board prototypes and using test equipment such as a DMM, oscilloscope and spectrum analyzer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Knowledge of C and Python for test firmware development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;English proficiency required; French and/or Dutch are a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Full EU working rights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
