&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Axon and be a Force for Good.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Axon, we’re on a mission to Protect Life. We’re explorers, pursuing society’s most critical safety and justice issues with our ecosystem of devices and cloud software. Like our products, we work better together. We connect with candor and care, seeking out diverse perspectives from our customers, communities and each other.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Life at Axon is fast-paced, challenging and meaningful. Here, you’ll take ownership and drive real change. Constantly grow as you work hard for a mission that matters at a company where you matter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Your Impact&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;As a Senior Product Manager, Dedrone, you will help define and execute the product strategy for the organization&#39;s Solution offerings. You will work at the intersection of customer needs, product strategy, and technical execution to shape how Dedrone products leverage RF, Radar, Camera, Networking, Software, and Firmware technologies to deploy, power, and operate systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who can translate mission and customer needs into clear requirements, contribute to a product roadmap, and drive alignment across engineering and business stakeholders while making thoughtful tradeoffs across performance, reliability, cost, power, and field quality. You will partner closely with electrical engineering, hardware engineering, systems engineering, RF engineering, firmware, software, operations, manufacturing, compliance, and external partners to ensure Dedrone&#39;s capabilities are robust and differentiated in real-world public safety environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Onsite at our Sterling, Virginia or Seattle Office 4 days a week&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to: Sr. Director of Product, Dedrone&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Reports: N/A&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to product strategy and own roadmap execution for defense solutions within Dedrone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define product requirements and prioritization for solution, hardware, and network design initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer, business, and operational needs into clear technical priorities for defense and counter-UAS field behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with external vendors and partners to support product strategy and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with RF, ME, EE, Firmware, Software, Compliance, Operations, and Supply Chain teams to drive end-to-end product decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure product decisions reflect real-world field conditions and solve problems in mission-critical environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive tradeoff decisions across BOM cost, system capabilities, schedule, manufacturability, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build alignment across cross-functional stakeholders and influence roadmap decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success metrics and use customer feedback, field data, and operational insights to improve product quality and connectivity outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer adoption of product features grows with high customer satisfaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product, business development, and engineering teams are aligned on high-value product investments and tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform decisions improve reliability, performance, and customer trust in real-world deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teams make earlier, better-informed decisions around certification, field quality, and launch readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer pain points tied to defense systems performance are better understood, prioritized, and reduced over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;3+ years of product management experience, with 1+ years in defense, public safety, counter-UAS, or technically complex hardware/software products; demonstrated ability to drive cross-functional alignment&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with wireless, embedded, or sensor domains — including some combination of RF, radar, camera, cellular, Wi-Fi, GNSS, or connectivity performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning or contributing to hardware products deployed in operationally demanding or mission-critical environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with system architecture documentation, hardware/software integration concepts, and multi-discipline technical stacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment and ability to prioritize across customer value, technical complexity, business impact, and execution risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in ambiguous, high-dependency environments with multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills and systems thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of delivering products or major capabilities with measurable customer and business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mission-critical, defense, cUAS, public safety, or other operationally demanding connected products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with hardware RF, radar, camera, network, embedded, or wireless systems engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Technical degree or MBA is a plus&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based out of our Sterling Office and follows a hybrid schedule. We rely on in-person collaboration and ask that team members work onsite Tuesdays through Fridays, with the flexibility to work remotely on Mondays, unless there is an approved workplace accommodation. We believe that connection fuels innovation, and our in-office culture is designed to foster meaningful teamwork, mentorship, and shared success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits that Benefit You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and 401k with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discretionary paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave for all&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, Dental, Vision plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fitness Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Emotional &amp;amp; Mental Wellness support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Resource Groups (ERGs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And yes, we have snacks in our offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits listed herein may vary depending on the nature of your employment and the location where you work.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Axon is a total compensation company, meaning compensation is made up of base pay, bonus, and stock awards. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: level, function, training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs, geographic market, and often a combination of all these factors. Our benefits offer an array of options to help support you physically, financially and emotionally through the big milestones and in your everyday life. To see more details on our benefits offerings please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.axon.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://www.axon.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$131,250&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$210,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Don’t meet every single requirement? That&#39;s ok. At Axon, we Aim Far. We think big with a long-term view because we want to reinvent the world to be a safer, better place. We are also committed to building diverse teams that reflect the communities we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Studies have shown that women and people of color are less likely to apply to jobs unless they check every box in the job description. If you’re excited about this role and our mission to Protect Life but your experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification listed here, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;/p&gt;
