&lt;p&gt;Axon Records is a cloud-based records management system that modernizes how law enforcement agencies capture, manage, and access data. It streamlines report writing and approval workflows with structured data entry, real-time collaboration, and intelligent automation. Our products north star is to make an impact on the world by reducing the amount of time officers spend at their desks writing reports and increase the amount of time officers spend out in their communities helping the public.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The International Squad is a full stack team that works across multiple areas of our products and focus on the internationalization and localization of features, extending them to suit the needs of international law enforcement agencies outside the United States. Expanding the adoption of our Records products to international customers is one of our key goals, and this squad is the main engineering team executing the work to make that happen.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;An ideal candidate would be a full stack developer who leans more towards the front-end, but also with back-end experience in micro services and distributed systems. In addition to writing code, the Sr Software Engineer is a role in which engineers are expected to set high technical standards for the team, mentor and train less experienced engineers and lead large and complex projects.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our team is looking for someone who excels at cross-team collaboration and can communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical partners. You should be comfortable building relationships across engineering teams to understand existing systems and make changes confidently and responsibly, while also partnering with stakeholders to translate customer and business needs into well-scoped technical work. This role requires the ability to explain tradeoffs, constraints, and project progress in a way that creates shared clarity—helping teams align on priorities, expectations, and delivery plans, especially when supporting customer go-lives and other time-sensitive initiatives.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Join us in making a meaningful impact on the lives of law enforcement and the communities they serve, as part of a passionate and mission-driven group dedicated to innovation and excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: This role is based out of our Seattle office and follows a hybrid schedule. We rely on in-person collaboration and ask that team members work onsite Tuesdays through Fridays, with the flexibility to work remotely on Mondays, unless there is an approved workplace accommodation. We believe that connection fuels innovation, and our in-office culture is designed to foster meaningful teamwork, mentorship, and shared success.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop scalable, secure, high-performance software in this mission-critical space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical projects from concept to launch, ensuring solution meets business and technical requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across teams with Product, Design, and Engineering to create solutions that delight our customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership and mentorship for engineers in the team and across the group&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help to define a technical vision both within our team and the greater organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engineering architecture design reviews and provide feedback to other engineers through channels like PR reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and review design documents, library proposals, and technical vision documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and manage roadmaps for the technical backlog&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously evaluate and improve engineering processes across the group to enhance efficiency and effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of professional software development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and delivering highly-available, scalable cloud-based systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in HTML, CSS, Typescript/Javascript and component-based frameworks such as React.js&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Back-end experience in languages such as Go, Scala , Java or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with SQL or NoSQL data stores&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;(Bonus) Experience with Docker, Kubernetes and CI/CD tooling such as TeamCity, Jenkins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;(Bonus) Experience with an automated testing framework like Selenium, Puppeteer, or Playwright or automated API testi&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits that Benefit You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and 401k with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discretionary paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave for all&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, Dental, Vision plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fitness Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Emotional &amp;amp; Mental Wellness support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And yes, we have snacks in our offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits listed herein may vary depending on the nature of your employment and the location where you work.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
